From: ihexon <zzheasy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: dw-hdmi: declare I2S audio playback-only

The DW HDMI I2S interface transmits audio to the HDMI sink; it does not
capture audio. Leaving no_i2s_capture unset exposes a capture PCM on
simple-card systems such as RK3399 EAIDK610. Opening it alongside playback
during audio profile probing hits hdmi-codec's single-stream guard.

Declare the actual direction instead of disabling HDMI or suppressing the
busy error. Analog codec capture is unaffected.

Signed-off-by: ihexon <zzheasy@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-i2s-audio.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-i2s-audio.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-i2s-audio.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-i2s-audio.c
@@ -197,6 +197,7 @@ static int snd_dw_hdmi_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	memset(&pdata, 0, sizeof(pdata));
 	pdata.ops		= &dw_hdmi_i2s_ops;
 	pdata.i2s		= 1;
+	pdata.no_i2s_capture	= 1;
 	pdata.max_i2s_channels	= 8;
 	pdata.data		= audio;
 
